    "__schema11": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": ["walk", "fly", "swim", "climb", "burrow"],
      "description": "- **walk**: Walk Speed is how far a creature can move on foot across open ground during its turn (e.g. 30 feet for most Medium humanoids).\n- **fly**: Fly Speed is how far a creature can move through the air. A creature without a Fly Speed cannot stay aloft unless a rule grants flight.\n- **swim**: Swim Speed is how far a creature can move through water. Without a Swim Speed, moving in water costs extra movement.\n- **climb**: Climb Speed is how far a creature can move while climbing. Without a Climb Speed, climbing costs extra movement.\n- **burrow**: Burrow Speed is how far a creature can move by tunneling through earth or loose material."
    },
